WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.232 --> 00:00:08.994
upon a time there lived a very wealthy merchant.

2
00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:11.235
He was not happy with his only son.

3
00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:16.759
The boy wasn't intelligent; he wasn't creative; and, even worse, he didn't like to work.

4
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.722
His mother loved him anyway, and she always made excuses for him.

5
00:00:22.523 --> 00:00:25.485
"He's not lazy," she would say to her husband.

6
00:00:25.505 --> 00:00:30.348
"He just takes his time because he wants everything to be perfect."

7
00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:36.214
Other times she would say, "Our son is intelligent.

8
00:00:36.694 --> 00:00:38.075
He hides it from others.

9
00:00:38.595 --> 00:00:41.277
He doesn't want to make his friends look stupid."

10
00:00:42.097 --> 00:00:46.039
The merchant didn't believe any of it, and he would just wave his wife away.

11
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:52.382
When the son was old enough to marry, the mother begged her husband to find him a wife.

12
00:00:53.103 --> 00:00:57.305
But the merchant thought his son was too stupid, too boring, and too lazy to marry.

13
00:00:58.526 --> 00:01:02.468
The boy's mother wanted him to marry, so she went to see her husband often.

14
00:01:04.116 --> 00:01:08.959
She told her husband that she believed her son possessed a large amount of wisdom and intelligence.

15
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.182
The merchant became angry with his wife, but she was too stubborn to notice.

16
00:01:15.102 --> 00:01:16.763
Finally he had had enough.

17
00:01:18.204 --> 00:01:19.605
"Look here," he said.

18
00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:22.586
"I have heard these stories many times.

19
00:01:23.127 --> 00:01:24.668
But you have never once proved them.

20
00:01:25.308 --> 00:01:26.188
Mothers are blind.

21
00:01:26.769 --> 00:01:28.570
I do not believe anything you have said.

22
00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.211
But it is too hot to argue.

23
00:01:31.692 --> 00:01:32.232
You have won.

24
00:01:33.096 --> 00:01:35.577
I will give that fool, our son, one more chance.

25
00:01:38.138 --> 00:01:39.838
"Give him this one small coin.

26
00:01:40.438 --> 00:01:41.699
Tell him to go to the market.

27
00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:44.799
I want him to buy a single item with the coin.

28
00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:52.422
That one item must be something to eat, something to drink, something to plant, and something to feed

29
00:01:52.582 --> 00:01:53.102
our goat."

30
00:01:54.722 --> 00:02:00.184
As the boy walked toward the market, he started to think, "What can I buy with this coin?

31
00:02:00.816 --> 00:02:04.159
Something to eat and drink and do all those other things?

32
00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.621
Surely this is impossible!"

33
00:02:08.543 --> 00:02:10.245
The boy sat down under a tree.

34
00:02:11.225 --> 00:02:13.167
He needed time to think and rest.

35
00:02:14.568 --> 00:02:17.391
As he was sitting there, the blacksmith's daughter came by.

36
00:02:18.131 --> 00:02:20.954
She looked at the boy and saw that he was very unhappy.

37
00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.695
"What's the matter?"

38
00:02:23.196 --> 00:02:23.716
she asked.

39
00:02:26.259 --> 00:02:31.014
The boy looked at her and said, "My father has given me an impossible task.

40
00:02:31.414 --> 00:02:34.335
He wants me to buy one item with this coin.

41
00:02:35.536 --> 00:02:42.380
And that item must be something to eat, something to drink, something to plant, and something to feed

42
00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:42.960
our goat."

43
00:02:44.941 --> 00:02:47.162
"I know what you can do," she said.

44
00:02:47.182 --> 00:02:50.264
"Go and buy a watermelon with the coin.

45
00:02:51.885 --> 00:02:54.266
It will provide everything your father said.

46
00:02:54.686 --> 00:02:57.628
Give it to him, and your parents will be pleased."

47
00:02:58.464 --> 00:02:59.124
The boy nodded.

48
00:02:59.804 --> 00:03:00.645
The girl was right!

49
00:03:01.205 --> 00:03:07.226
His family could eat the watermelon, drink its juice, plant its seeds, and feed its rind to their

50
00:03:07.266 --> 00:03:09.307
goat. "Thanks," he said.

51
00:03:10.227 --> 00:03:13.488
The boy ran to the market and got a watermelon for his father.

52
00:03:14.308 --> 00:03:18.129
When the merchant's wife saw her son's cleverness, she was very pleased.

53
00:03:18.149 --> 00:03:23.151
"Look," she said to her husband, "our son has succeeded."

54
00:03:23.171 --> 00:03:27.752
"Actually, Mom," said the boy, "I had help.

55
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:32.464
Without the advice of the blacksmith's daughter, I would have failed."

56
00:03:33.605 --> 00:03:34.786
The father was impressed.

57
00:03:35.446 --> 00:03:39.710
His son hadn't found the solution by himself, but he was honest enough to admit it.

58
00:03:41.732 --> 00:03:43.233
Honesty was a worthy quality.

59
00:03:44.114 --> 00:03:48.518
The merchant was satisfied that his son would make a good husband because he was honest.

60
00:03:49.619 --> 00:03:51.921
He invited the blacksmith and his family for dinner.

61
00:03:53.082 --> 00:03:55.524
The families decided their son and daughter would marry.

62
00:03:56.748 --> 00:04:00.591
The blacksmith was glad that his daughter would marry into such a wealthy family.

63
00:04:01.572 --> 00:04:06.015
The merchant's son and the blacksmith's daughter were happy because they made a good team.

64
00:04:08.617 --> 00:04:10.558
The boy became a hardworking husband.

65
00:04:11.479 --> 00:04:16.483
The boy's father was glad that he had given his son another chance, and the boy's mother was

66
00:04:16.543 --> 00:04:22.868
happy because her son was wise, honest, and hardworking, just as she always knew he was.
